FAULT(1)

NAME
    fault - trigger a controlled user fault

SYNOPSIS
    fault [ud|gp|de|br|bp|of|pf]

DESCRIPTION
    Used to verify kernel fault handling for user processes.  Each mode
    triggers a controlled CPU exception and lets the kernel terminate only
    the faulting process.

    After a run, cat /proc/lastfault to inspect the kernel's latest fault
    snapshot.

NOTES
    This is primarily a diagnostic or self-test helper, but it is documented so installed programs are discoverable.
